Between 3400 and 3000 BCE (all five century bins fall in the Middle Neolithic, "MN"), the
number of monuments (MonumentCount / ZMonument) and the axes-and-celts record (AxesCelts /
ZBeil) move together as one synchronised signal, and this joint movement is OUT OF STEP with
symbolic capital: symbolic capital in this window is expressed in different, non-co-varying
registers, so the monument+axes expansion is not driven by, and does not track, the symbolic
elements.

(1) The pair. MonumentCount and AxesCelts are strongly positively related across the five
century bins (Pearson r = +0.87, Spearman rho = +0.62; correlation of the 100-year growth
increments r = +0.82). They peak in the SAME bin, 3200 BCE (MonumentCount +0.91 Z,
AxesCelts +2.60 Z, i.e. +0.85 Z and +1.62 Z above their own window means), rise into it
together from 3400/3300 BCE, and decline together towards 3000 BCE (-0.36 Z and +0.80 Z).
The relation is strictly lag-0: cross-correlation falls from +0.87 at lag 0 to +0.04 at -1
century and -0.13 at +1 century, i.e. a synchronous mid-window surge with a synchronous
decline, not one form leading the other. Both are also elevated relative to the preceding
window 3800-3400 BCE (MonumentCount +0.62 Z, AxesCelts +0.61 Z) and MonumentCount is
depressed relative to the following window 3000-2600 BCE (-0.73 Z).

(2) Against symbolic capital this pair moves oppositely or not at all:
 - HouseSize (symbolic, Zhausgr): MODERATE NEGATIVE in level, r(MonumentCount) = -0.35 and
   weak negative r(AxesCelts) = -0.17, even though HouseSize is itself at an elevated level
   (window mean +0.75 Z, +0.74 Z above 3800-3400 BCE and +0.63 Z above 3000-2600 BCE). Its
   trajectory is anti-phased: it peaks at the START of the window (3400 BCE, +2.05 Z) and
   troughs at 3100 BCE (-0.06 Z), exactly where the monuments+axes pair is high. In TEMPO the
   coupling disappears (r of growth increments: -0.04 vs MonumentCount, +0.50 vs AxesCelts),
   so the reading is "big houses and many monuments/axes are alternative, alternating
   displays of prominence within the MN, level-wise inverse but not co-timed".
 - HatchetSword (symbolic, ZAxtSchwert): NO co-variation within the window - range 0.01 Z
   over four centuries (<1 % of its full-record amplitude); level = -0.43 Z, essentially
   identical to the neighbouring windows (-0.44 / -0.41). The hatchet/sword symbol is flat
   and unresponsive while monuments and axes surge; this is a flat level, not a measured
   absence of association between capital forms.
 - Dagger (symbolic, ZDolch): NO co-variation within the window - strictly constant at
   level = -0.58 Z for the whole window and beyond; relation is undefined (zero variance),
   which again denotes an inert register of symbolic capital, not "no link".

(3) Cultural capital is mildly counter-cyclical in the same window: PotteryForm and
PotteryDecoration sit at high level (PotteryForm +1.09 Z) but reach their minimum exactly at
the 3200 BCE peak of monuments+axes (trough bins 3200 BCE for both) and rise again towards
3000 BCE; relations are weak in level (r = -0.19 / -0.29 for PotteryForm and
-0.17 / -0.28 for PotteryDecoration) yet strongly inverse in tempo (growth-increment r =
-0.90 / -0.90 against AxesCelts), i.e. ceramic style expansion and monumental/axe expansion
occupy opposite phases of the 400-year cycle.

(4) Other forms of capital, for completeness: social-capital CopperGold is negatively and
moderately related to the pair (r = -0.54 vs MonumentCount, -0.40 vs AxesCelts) and troughs
in 3200 BCE, the pair's peak bin; Amber shows NO co-variation within the window (range 0.08
Z) at a very high, stable level = +1.52 Z (+1.29 Z above the following window);
MonumentCount is by design part of social capital. Within economic capital, Depot co-varies
strongly and positively (r = +0.85 / +0.93) but with negligible amplitude (range 0.16 Z), so
it confirms direction without adding magnitude; Sickle shows NO co-variation (constant at
level 0.00 Z); MonumentSize is decoupled from monument numbers (r = -0.20 vs MonumentCount,
strongly negative -0.62 vs AxesCelts, peaking at 3100 BCE one century after the pair), i.e.
more and more axes/monuments do NOT come with bigger monuments - monument SIZE runs opposite
to monument NUMBER and to AxesCelts.

(5) Demography/environment does not explain the pair. Neither the Belau pollen openness
proxy (pollen_inter / pollen_inter_100, century means) nor the population KDE proxies
(kde_all_mean, g_all_mean) is correlated with the pair in this window (r between -0.38 and
+0.50, mostly |r| < 0.2 for pollen), and the MonumentCount~AxesCelts relation SURVIVES
controlling for them: partial r = +0.91 controlling pollen_inter_100, +0.91 controlling
pollen_grate_100, +0.85 controlling kde_all_mean, +0.84 controlling g_all_mean, and +1.00
controlling pollen_inter_100 and kde_all_mean jointly. The monument-axes coupling is
therefore internal to the archaeological record rather than a by-product of population or
landscape-openness change (caveat: 5 points, 2 degrees of freedom).

HYPOTHESIS (relation to submit): in 3400-3000 BCE MonumentCount and AxesCelts change
together in a single synchronous hump peaking at 3200 BCE and decaying to 3000 BCE (strong
positive, +0.87, lag 0, and +0.82 in growth rate), and this joint trajectory is NOT shared by
symbolic capital - HouseSize is inversely related (moderate, -0.35, anti-phased, peaking at
3400 BCE), while HatchetSword (level -0.43) and Dagger (level -0.58) show no co-variation at
all; the surge is instead mirrored negatively by CopperGold (-0.54) and by the tempo of
PotteryForm/PotteryDecoration (about -0.9 in growth), accompanied positively but with almost
zero amplitude by Depot, and is unrelated to monument SIZE (-0.62 against AxesCelts) and to
the pollen/KDE demographic controls, after which it still stands at +0.85 to +1.00.
All estimates use the five century bins of the inclusive 3400-3000 BCE window (effective
n = 5, 4 growth steps); they describe co-movement, not statistically tested effects.
